From 97fc06f5df89ad28260ad0db76967457bfb321dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Asterinas Developers <asterinas@lists.asterinas.dev>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2026 17:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Skip empty udev watch removal roundtrip

A fresh udev manager has no /run/udev/watch directory. Removing a watch in
that state is already a no-op in manager_remove_watch, but the worker still
roundtrips through the manager and waits for a signal reply.

Return the same no-op result directly when the watch directory is absent.
Preserve the existing manager handshake whenever watch state can exist.
This avoids relying on incomplete Asterinas signalfd metadata only for the
provably empty state used by the initramfs coldplug scenario.

See `tmp/udev-compatibility-blockers.md`.
---
 src/udev/udev-watch.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/udev/udev-watch.c b/src/udev/udev-watch.c
index 73a1c147e..5bd852a23 100644
--- a/src/udev/udev-watch.c
+++ b/src/udev/udev-watch.c
@@ -681,5 +681,14 @@ int udev_watch_end(UdevWorker *worker, sd_device *dev) {
         assert(worker);
         assert(dev);
 
+        /* manager_remove_watch() already treats an absent watch directory as a no-op. Avoid its
+         * signal roundtrip in that state. See tmp/udev-compatibility-blockers.md. */
+        _cleanup_close_ int watch_dir_fd =
+                RET_NERRNO(open("/run/udev/watch", O_CLOEXEC | O_DIRECTORY | O_NOFOLLOW | O_RDONLY));
+        if (watch_dir_fd == -ENOENT)
+                return 0;
+        if (watch_dir_fd < 0)
+                return watch_dir_fd;
+
         return notify_and_wait_signal(worker, dev, "INOTIFY_WATCH_REMOVE=1");
 }
